findings.claim:
To pass the zero-tolerance check, v6 draws every tapped hole at the thread's outer (major) diameter. In the drawn pose this hides no overlap. But it removes all thread information from the package:
- the STEP files and drawing sheets show plain Ø3.0, Ø2.5, Ø4 and Ø12 holes, under the sheets' general tolerance 'holes +0.2/0';
- no note or drawing calls out a thread;
- the hub's part note still describes the old COB build and lists none of its holes.
A shop working from this package would drill those holes to the drawn size and leave nothing to tap. The check also no longer tests how far each thread engages or whether a blind hole is deep enough; the pins' threads end exactly at the bottom of their holes.

